title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1926 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/Inter_Party.png
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Poland.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The PPS cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties. We have only been able to enter governments consisting of the PSL-W, PSL-P, and other Democratic parties. We can reach out and build additional connections with these parties, or perhaps we can stand alone.

- @peasant: Strengthen our bonds with the **<span style="color: #80FF00;">PSL-"Liberation"</span>** and left-agrarian **<span style="color: #179900;">PSL-"Left"</span>**.
- @piast: Strengthen our bonds with the conservative **<span style="color: #3A6538;">PSL-"Piast"</span>**.
- @bmn: Strengthen our bonds with centrist **<span style="color: #E3AF34;">Minority Parties</span>**.
- @kpp: Work towards repairing relationships with the KPP
- @pps_alone: The PPS can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard

@peasant
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; psl_l_relation += 8; psl_w_relation += 8

We are ideologically close with them so it is easy to build relations with the PSL-L.

@piast
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: lanckorona if lanckorona_pact = 1; piast_op_2 if psl_p_in_government = 0 and pps_in_government = 0; piast_op if psl_p_in_government = 1 and pps_in_government = 0; piast_coalition if pps_in_government = 1 and psl_p_in_government = 1

@piast_op
on-arrival: psl_p_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); psl_p_relation += 2*(1 - dissent) if pps_toleration; psl_p_left += 0.5

[? if pps_toleration != 1 : We are currently in opposition to the current government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will. ?][? if pps_toleration : We are currently tolerating the government, so we are able to build relations with them. ?]

@piast_op_2
on-arrival: piast_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); psl_p_left += 0.5

Together with the <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>, we share a common opposition to the incumbent cabinet, making improving relations easier.

@piast_coalition
on-arrival: psl_p_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); psl_p_left += 1

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@lanckorona
on-arrival: psl_p_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); psl_p_left += 0.5

The rightward turn of the PSL-P has made building relations difficult, but not impossible

@bmn
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; bmn_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: bmn_coalition if bmn_in_government and pps_in_government = 1

We are able through build a relationship with the BMN.

@bmn_coalition
on-arrival: bmn_relation += 3*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, and historically, they haven't been able to enter the government without our help so improving relations comes naturally.

@kpp
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; kpp_relation += 10

Here you go 10 KPP relations for FREE

@pps_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
